{"name":"Jam Session","hex":"#d4cfd6","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"jam session","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An informal gathering of musicians to play music, especially improvised jazz or a similar genre."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/jam_session"}],"entries":[{"title":"Jam Session (1942 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Jam Session is a 1942 American short film, directed by Josef Berne, which shows Duke Ellington and his orchestra performing \"C Jam Blues\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/09/Jam_Session_%281942%29.webm/330px--Jam_Session_%281942%29.webm.jpg","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jam_Session_(1942_film)"},{"title":"Jam Session (1944 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Jam Session is a 1944 American musical film starring Ann Miller."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jam_Session_(1944_film)"},{"title":"Jam session","blocks":[{"text":"A jam session is a relatively informal musical event, process, or activity where musicians, typically instrumentalists, play improvised solos and vamp over tunes, drones, songs, and chord progressions. To \"jam\" is to improvise music without extensive preparation or predefined arrangements. Original jam sessions, also called \"free flow sessions,\" are often used by musicians to develop new material (music) and find suitable arrangements. Both styles can be used simply as a social gathering and communal practice session. Jam sessions may be based upon existing songs or forms, may be loosely based on an agreed chord progression or chart suggested by one participant, or may be wholly improvisational. Jam sessions can range from very loose gatherings of amateurs to evenings where a jam session coordinator or host acts as a \"gatekeeper\" so that appropriate-level performers take the stage to sophisticated improvised recording sessions by professionals which are intended to be broadcast live on radio or TV or edited and released to the public."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4e/Bluegrass_Music_Jam_Delafield_Fish_Hatchery_Wisconsin_February_2009.jpg/330px-Bluegrass_Music_Jam_Delafield_Fish_Hatchery_Wisconsin_February_2009.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jam_session"},{"title":"Fruit preserves","blocks":[{"text":"Fruit preserves are preparations of fruits whose main preserving agent is sugar and sometimes acid, often stored in glass jars and used as a condiment or spread."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/21/Fruits_jam_variants.jpg/330px-Fruits_jam_variants.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fruit_preserves"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/56/CK5_rocking_the_light_board.jpg/500px-CK5_rocking_the_light_board.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/56/CK5_rocking_the_light_board.jpg/1280px-CK5_rocking_the_light_board.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/56/CK5_rocking_the_light_board.jpg/500px-CK5_rocking_the_light_board.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":" Phish is an example of a \"jam band\".","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACK5_rocking_the_light_board.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/Bluegrass_pickin%27.jpg/500px-Bluegrass_pickin%27.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/Bluegrass_pickin%27.jpg/1280px-Bluegrass_pickin%27.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/